  user_input {
    user_response: "Act as a senior MERN stack developer and a beginner-friendly mentor.\n\nI am building the VELoop Rewards full-stack assignment.\n\nRequired technology:\n- Frontend: React + Vite\n- Styling: Bootstrap + CSS Modules\n- Backend: Node.js + Express\n- Database: MongoDB + Mongoose\n- Icons: Lucide React\n\nThe project must contain:\n1. A user profile dashboard at `/user-profile`.\n2. A protected admin management panel.\n3. Secure authentication and role-based authorization.\n4. Working APIs connected to MongoDB.\n5. Testing, deployment and all required documentation.\n\nFor now, complete **Phase 1: Planning ONLY**.\n\nPlease provide:\n1. Complete project architecture.\n2. Frontend and backend folder structure.\n3. Database models and relationships.\n4. API endpoint list.\n5. Authentication and security approach.\n6. Development phases in the correct order.\n7. Required environment variables.\n\nImportant:\n- Do not write code yet.\n- Do not invent VELoop\'s actual wallet rules, APIs or reward conversion logic.\n- Clearly identify information that needs confirmation.\n- Explain everything in simple language suitable for a beginner.\n- Prioritize functional backend integration and secure data handling.\n\nWait for my approval before starting Phase 2."
    items {
      text: "Act as a senior MERN stack developer and a beginner-friendly mentor.\n\nI am building the VELoop Rewards full-stack assignment.\n\nRequired technology:\n- Frontend: React + Vite\n- Styling: Bootstrap + CSS Modules\n- Backend: Node.js + Express\n- Database: MongoDB + Mongoose\n- Icons: Lucide React\n\nThe project must contain:\n1. A user profile dashboard at `/user-profile`.\n2. A protected admin management panel.\n3. Secure authentication and role-based authorization.\n4. Working APIs connected to MongoDB.\n5. Testing, deployment and all required documentation.\n\nFor now, complete **Phase 1: Planning ONLY**.\n\nPlease provide:\n1. Complete project architecture.\n2. Frontend and backend folder structure.\n3. Database models and relationships.\n4. API endpoint list.\n5. Authentication and security approach.\n6. Development phases in the correct order.\n7. Required environment variables.\n\nImportant:\n- Do not write code yet.\n- Do not invent VELoop\'s actual wallet rules, APIs or reward conversion logic.\n- Clearly identify information that needs confirmation.\n- Explain everything in simple language suitable for a beginner.\n- Prioritize functional backend integration and secure data handling.\n\nWait for my approval before starting Phase 2."
    }
  }
}
