  planner_response {
    response: "Welcome to your MERN stack internship assignment! As your technical mentor, I am thrilled to guide you step-by-step through building **VELoop Rewards \342\200\223 User Profile & Admin Management System**.\n\nBelow is the comprehensive **Phase 1: Project Planning** breakdown, explained in beginner-friendly language.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Complete Project Architecture\n\nOur application follows the standard **MERN (MongoDB, Express.js, React, Node.js)** full-stack architecture:\n* **Frontend (React + Vite)**: Runs in the user\'s browser. It handles UI rendering, user interaction, routing, and communicating with our backend API via HTTP requests (using `fetch` or `axios`).\n* **Backend (Node.js + Express.js)**: Acts as our server. It receives requests from the frontend, validates user sessions, processes business logic, and talks to the database.\n* **Database (MongoDB + Mongoose)**: Stores all persistent data (users, wallets, transactions, level configurations, achievements, and admin audit logs).\n* **Integration**: We connect the frontend and backend together in a unified Node server (`server.ts`) that serves both our Express API routes and our Vite development/production frontend.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Frontend and Backend Folder Structure\n\n```text\nveloop-rewards/\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server.ts                  # Main Node.js & Express server entry point\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json               # Project dependencies and npm scripts\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 .env.example               # Template for required environment variables\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server/                    # Backend (Node.js + Express + Mongoose)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 config/                # Database connection setup\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 models/                # Mongoose database schemas\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 routes/                # REST API endpoints\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 middleware/            # JWT authentication & admin authorization\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 data/                  # Fallback in-memory store for offline reliability\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 seed.ts                # Database seeder for demo accounts\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/                       # Frontend (React + Vite + Tailwind/CSS Modules)\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 assets/                # Images and icons\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/            # Reusable UI components (ProfileHero, RewardAssets, LevelProgress, etc.)\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 pages/                 # Full pages (Login, UserProfile, AdminLogin, AdminDashboard)\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 context/               # React Context for global auth state\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 utils/                 # Helper functions (clipboard copy, formatting)\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 App.tsx                # Main router component\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 main.tsx               # React DOM entry point\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Database Models and Relationships\n\nUsing **Mongoose**, we define structured schemas for MongoDB:\n1. **User**: Stores member credentials (`username`, `email`, `passwordHash`, `referralCode`, `status`).\n2. **Wallet**: Linked to a User (`userId`). Stores balances for **VEs**, **SVEs**, **Gems**, **Tokens**, and **XP**.\n3. **WalletTransaction**: Logs every credit, debit, or adjustment to a user\'s wallet with an audit trail.\n4. **LevelConfig**: Defines level thresholds, names, and badge requirements.\n5. **Achievement & UserAchievement**: Tracks platform achievements and which users have unlocked them.\n6. **Referral**: Links referrers to referred users and tracks bonuses earned.\n7. **Withdrawal**: Tracks user withdrawal requests and approval status (`pending`, `approved`, `rejected`).\n8. **ActivityLog**: Records recent actions (daily bonus, XP gained, withdrawals).\n9. **AdminUser & AdminAuditLog**: Stores administrative credentials and logs every administrative action (suspending users, adjusting balances).\n\n---\n\n### 4. API Endpoint List\n\n#### Authentication APIs\n* `POST /api/auth/register` \342\200\224 Register a new member account\n* `POST /api/auth/login` \342\200\224 Sign in a member\n* `GET /api/auth/me` \342\200\224 Verify current user session\n\n#### User Profile APIs\n* `GET /api/profile/me` \342\200\224 Get user profile details\n* `PATCH /api/profile/me` \342\200\224 Update permitted profile fields\n* `GET /api/profile/rewards` \342\200\224 Fetch wallet balances for VEs, SVEs, Gems, Tokens, XP\n* `GET /api/profile/level-progress` \342\200\224 Fetch current level progress and next milestone\n* `GET /api/profile/achievements` \342\200\224 Fetch unlocked and upcoming achievements\n* `GET /api/profile/withdrawal-summary` \342\200\224 Fetch withdrawal history and status totals\n* `GET /api/profile/referrals` \342\200\224 Fetch referral snapshot and statistics\n* `GET /api/profile/activity` \342\200\224 Fetch recent user activity feed\n\n#### Admin Management APIs\n* `POST /api/admin/auth/login` \342\200\224 Admin sign-in (demo: `admin@veloop.io` / `Admin@123`)\n* `GET /api/admin/stats` \342\200\224 Platform overview statistics\n* `GET /api/admin/users` \342\200\224 Paginated user list with search & filter\n* `PATCH /api/admin/users/:id/status` \342\200\224 Suspend or restore user accounts\n* `POST /api/admin/rewards/adjust` \342\200\224 Adjust user wallet balances (with mandatory audit log)\n* `GET /api/admin/withdrawals` \342\200\224 View withdrawal requests\n* `PATCH /api/admin/withdrawals/:id/status` \342\200\224 Approve or reject withdrawal requests\n* `GET /api/admin/audit-logs` \342\200\224 View system administration audit trails\n\n---\n\n### 5. Authentication and Security Approach\n\n* **Password Hashing**: Passwords are never stored in plaintext. We use `bcryptjs` to hash passwords securely before saving them to MongoDB.\n* **JWT (JSON Web Tokens)**: Upon successful login, the server issues a signed JWT token. The frontend stores this token and sends it in the `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header for protected requests.\n* **Role-Based Authorization**: Middleware checks if the request comes from an authenticated user or an authorized administrator (`isAdmin: true`). Normal users cannot access admin routes or modify wallet balances.\n* **Server-Side Validation**: All critical business logic (wallet balances, XP gain, level calculation) is enforced on the backend. Frontend inputs are never blindly trusted.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Development Phases in the Correct Order\n\n1. **Phase 1: Project Planning** *(Current Phase)*\n2. **Phase 2: Database Models & Backend APIs** (Setting up Express server, Mongoose models, authentication middleware, and seed scripts).\n3. **Phase 3: Frontend Layout & Components** (Building React router, context, ProfileHero, RewardAssets, and dashboard pages).\n4. **Phase 4: API Integration** (Connecting React components to backend REST endpoints with loading and error states).\n5. **Phase 5: Protected Admin Panel** (Building admin login, user management, reward adjustment, and withdrawal approvals).\n6. **Phase 6: Security & Testing** (Verifying role restrictions, authentication flows, and data integrity).\n7. **Phase 7: Documentation & Deployment** (Writing `README.md`, `API_DOCUMENTATION.md`, `DEMO_ACCESS.md`, and deploying).\n\n---\n\n### 7. Required Environment Variables\n\n```env\nPORT=3000\nMONGO_URI=\"mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/veloop_rewards\"\nJWT_SECRET=\"veloop_secure_jwt_secret_key_2026\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Information That Needs Confirmation (VELoop Platform Rules)\nBecause VELoop is a simulated/assignment rewards platform:\n- *Exact Payout Channels*: We implement standard simulated wallet addresses (`0x...` or bank accounts) for withdrawal requests.\n- *Conversion Ratios*: We treat VEs, SVEs, Gems, Tokens, and XP as independent platform assets managed via backend configuration.\n\nPlease review this Phase 1 plan and let me know if you would like to proceed to **Phase 2: Backend Implementation & Database Models**!"
    thinking: "**Defining Project Architecture**\n\nI\'ve finalized the project\'s architecture plan! It\'s now securely stored, and I\'m ready for the next phase, pending your feedback. The complete implementation plan is ready, as per your request.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Welcome to your MERN stack internship assignment! As your technical mentor, I am thrilled to guide you step-by-step through building **VELoop Rewards \342\200\223 User Profile & Admin Management System**.\n\nBelow is the comprehensive **Phase 1: Project Planning** breakdown, explained in beginner-friendly language.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Complete Project Architecture\n\nOur application follows the standard **MERN (MongoDB, Express.js, React, Node.js)** full-stack architecture:\n* **Frontend (React + Vite)**: Runs in the user\'s browser. It handles UI rendering, user interaction, routing, and communicating with our backend API via HTTP requests (using `fetch` or `axios`).\n* **Backend (Node.js + Express.js)**: Acts as our server. It receives requests from the frontend, validates user sessions, processes business logic, and talks to the database.\n* **Database (MongoDB + Mongoose)**: Stores all persistent data (users, wallets, transactions, level configurations, achievements, and admin audit logs).\n* **Integration**: We connect the frontend and backend together in a unified Node server (`server.ts`) that serves both our Express API routes and our Vite development/production frontend.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Frontend and Backend Folder Structure\n\n```text\nveloop-rewards/\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server.ts                  # Main Node.js & Express server entry point\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json               # Project dependencies and npm scripts\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 .env.example               # Template for required environment variables\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server/                    # Backend (Node.js + Express + Mongoose)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 config/                # Database connection setup\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 models/                # Mongoose database schemas\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 routes/                # REST API endpoints\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 middleware/            # JWT authentication & admin authorization\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 data/                  # Fallback in-memory store for offline reliability\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 seed.ts                # Database seeder for demo accounts\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/                       # Frontend (React + Vite + Tailwind/CSS Modules)\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 assets/                # Images and icons\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/            # Reusable UI components (ProfileHero, RewardAssets, LevelProgress, etc.)\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 pages/                 # Full pages (Login, UserProfile, AdminLogin, AdminDashboard)\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 context/               # React Context for global auth state\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 utils/                 # Helper functions (clipboard copy, formatting)\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 App.tsx                # Main router component\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 main.tsx               # React DOM entry point\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Database Models and Relationships\n\nUsing **Mongoose**, we define structured schemas for MongoDB:\n1. **User**: Stores member credentials (`username`, `email`, `passwordHash`, `referralCode`, `status`).\n2. **Wallet**: Linked to a User (`userId`). Stores balances for **VEs**, **SVEs**, **Gems**, **Tokens**, and **XP**.\n3. **WalletTransaction**: Logs every credit, debit, or adjustment to a user\'s wallet with an audit trail.\n4. **LevelConfig**: Defines level thresholds, names, and badge requirements.\n5. **Achievement & UserAchievement**: Tracks platform achievements and which users have unlocked them.\n6. **Referral**: Links referrers to referred users and tracks bonuses earned.\n7. **Withdrawal**: Tracks user withdrawal requests and approval status (`pending`, `approved`, `rejected`).\n8. **ActivityLog**: Records recent actions (daily bonus, XP gained, withdrawals).\n9. **AdminUser & AdminAuditLog**: Stores administrative credentials and logs every administrative action (suspending users, adjusting balances).\n\n---\n\n### 4. API Endpoint List\n\n#### Authentication APIs\n* `POST /api/auth/register` \342\200\224 Register a new member account\n* `POST /api/auth/login` \342\200\224 Sign in a member\n* `GET /api/auth/me` \342\200\224 Verify current user session\n\n#### User Profile APIs\n* `GET /api/profile/me` \342\200\224 Get user profile details\n* `PATCH /api/profile/me` \342\200\224 Update permitted profile fields\n* `GET /api/profile/rewards` \342\200\224 Fetch wallet balances for VEs, SVEs, Gems, Tokens, XP\n* `GET /api/profile/level-progress` \342\200\224 Fetch current level progress and next milestone\n* `GET /api/profile/achievements` \342\200\224 Fetch unlocked and upcoming achievements\n* `GET /api/profile/withdrawal-summary` \342\200\224 Fetch withdrawal history and status totals\n* `GET /api/profile/referrals` \342\200\224 Fetch referral snapshot and statistics\n* `GET /api/profile/activity` \342\200\224 Fetch recent user activity feed\n\n#### Admin Management APIs\n* `POST /api/admin/auth/login` \342\200\224 Admin sign-in (demo: `admin@veloop.io` / `Admin@123`)\n* `GET /api/admin/stats` \342\200\224 Platform overview statistics\n* `GET /api/admin/users` \342\200\224 Paginated user list with search & filter\n* `PATCH /api/admin/users/:id/status` \342\200\224 Suspend or restore user accounts\n* `POST /api/admin/rewards/adjust` \342\200\224 Adjust user wallet balances (with mandatory audit log)\n* `GET /api/admin/withdrawals` \342\200\224 View withdrawal requests\n* `PATCH /api/admin/withdrawals/:id/status` \342\200\224 Approve or reject withdrawal requests\n* `GET /api/admin/audit-logs` \342\200\224 View system administration audit trails\n\n---\n\n### 5. Authentication and Security Approach\n\n* **Password Hashing**: Passwords are never stored in plaintext. We use `bcryptjs` to hash passwords securely before saving them to MongoDB.\n* **JWT (JSON Web Tokens)**: Upon successful login, the server issues a signed JWT token. The frontend stores this token and sends it in the `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header for protected requests.\n* **Role-Based Authorization**: Middleware checks if the request comes from an authenticated user or an authorized administrator (`isAdmin: true`). Normal users cannot access admin routes or modify wallet balances.\n* **Server-Side Validation**: All critical business logic (wallet balances, XP gain, level calculation) is enforced on the backend. Frontend inputs are never blindly trusted.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Development Phases in the Correct Order\n\n1. **Phase 1: Project Planning** *(Current Phase)*\n2. **Phase 2: Database Models & Backend APIs** (Setting up Express server, Mongoose models, authentication middleware, and seed scripts).\n3. **Phase 3: Frontend Layout & Components** (Building React router, context, ProfileHero, RewardAssets, and dashboard pages).\n4. **Phase 4: API Integration** (Connecting React components to backend REST endpoints with loading and error states).\n5. **Phase 5: Protected Admin Panel** (Building admin login, user management, reward adjustment, and withdrawal approvals).\n6. **Phase 6: Security & Testing** (Verifying role restrictions, authentication flows, and data integrity).\n7. **Phase 7: Documentation & Deployment** (Writing `README.md`, `API_DOCUMENTATION.md`, `DEMO_ACCESS.md`, and deploying).\n\n---\n\n### 7. Required Environment Variables\n\n```env\nPORT=3000\nMONGO_URI=\"mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/veloop_rewards\"\nJWT_SECRET=\"veloop_secure_jwt_secret_key_2026\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Information That Needs Confirmation (VELoop Platform Rules)\nBecause VELoop is a simulated/assignment rewards platform:\n- *Exact Payout Channels*: We implement standard simulated wallet addresses (`0x...` or bank accounts) for withdrawal requests.\n- *Conversion Ratios*: We treat VEs, SVEs, Gems, Tokens, and XP as independent platform assets managed via backend configuration.\n\nPlease review this Phase 1 plan and let me know if you would like to proceed to **Phase 2: Backend Implementation & Database Models**!"
