    user_response: "The Phase 1 architecture is reviewed. Before starting Phase 2, apply these corrections:\n\n1. Use Bootstrap and CSS Modules, not Tailwind.\n2. Keep frontend (React + Vite) and backend (Node.js + Express) in separate folders.\n3. Do not use an in-memory fallback as a replacement for MongoDB.\n4. Use secure authentication and authorization practices.\n5. Never hardcode admin credentials or production secrets.\n6. Add missing admin API requirements for user details, levels, achievements, referrals and activity logs.\n7. Keep unknown VELoop business rules configurable. Do not invent wallet conversion ratios, withdrawal rules, XP calculations or referral bonuses.\n\nNow begin Phase 2, but work only on the first milestone:\n\n**Milestone 1: Backend foundation**\n- Initialize the backend project.\n- Install required dependencies.\n- Configure Express.\n- Configure MongoDB using Mongoose.\n- Add environment variable handling.\n- Add a health-check endpoint.\n- Add proper error handling.\n\nGive me exact terminal commands and explain each file in beginner-friendly language.\n\nDo not start frontend development yet. After completing this milestone, provide testing instructions and wait for my approval."
    items {
      text: "The Phase 1 architecture is reviewed. Before starting Phase 2, apply these corrections:\n\n1. Use Bootstrap and CSS Modules, not Tailwind.\n2. Keep frontend (React + Vite) and backend (Node.js + Express) in separate folders.\n3. Do not use an in-memory fallback as a replacement for MongoDB.\n4. Use secure authentication and authorization practices.\n5. Never hardcode admin credentials or production secrets.\n6. Add missing admin API requirements for user details, levels, achievements, referrals and activity logs.\n7. Keep unknown VELoop business rules configurable. Do not invent wallet conversion ratios, withdrawal rules, XP calculations or referral bonuses.\n\nNow begin Phase 2, but work only on the first milestone:\n\n**Milestone 1: Backend foundation**\n- Initialize the backend project.\n- Install required dependencies.\n- Configure Express.\n- Configure MongoDB using Mongoose.\n- Add environment variable handling.\n- Add a health-check endpoint.\n- Add proper error handling.\n\nGive me exact terminal commands and explain each file in beginner-friendly language.\n\nDo not start frontend development yet. After completing this milestone, provide testing instructions and wait for my approval."
    }
