  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed **Phase 2, Milestone 1: Backend Foundation**.\n\n---\n\n### File Explanations (Beginner-Friendly Guide)\n\n1. **`backend/package.json`**:\n   - Defines our backend project metadata, scripts (`npm start` and `npm run dev`), and required dependencies (`express`, `mongoose`, `dotenv`, `cors`, `cookie-parser`, `bcryptjs`, `jsonwebtoken`).\n2. **`backend/.env.example`**:\n   - A template for environment variables (`PORT`, `MONGO_URI`, `JWT_SECRET`). This ensures we never hardcode secrets in source code.\n3. **`backend/src/config/db.js`**:\n   - Uses **Mongoose** to connect our Node.js server to our MongoDB database cluster using the `MONGO_URI` connection string.\n4. **`backend/src/middleware/errorHandler.js`**:\n   - A centralized Express middleware that catches any errors occurring in our application and returns a clean, secure JSON error response.\n5. **`backend/src/server.js`**:\n   - The main entry point. It creates our Express app, applies security and parsing middleware (`cors`, `express.json`, `cookie-parser`), connects to MongoDB, provides the health-check endpoint (`GET /api/health`), attaches the error handler, and starts listening on port 5000.\n\n---\n\n### Exact Terminal Commands to Run\n\nTo test Milestone 1, open your terminal and execute the following commands inside the `backend` directory:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Navigate to the backend directory\ncd backend\n\n# 2. Install dependencies\nnpm install\n\n# 3. Create your local .env file from the template\ncp .env.example .env\n\n# 4. Start the backend server in development mode\nnpm run dev\n```\n\n---\n\n### How to Test the Health-Check Endpoint\n\nOnce the server is running, open your browser or Postman and test:\n```text\nhttp://localhost:5000/api/health\n```\n**Expected Response:**\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"UP\",\n  \"message\": \"VELoop Rewards Backend API is running successfully\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T...\"\n}\n```\n\nPlease review and test Milestone 1, and reply with your approval to proceed to **Milestone 2: Database Models & Authentication APIs**."
    modified_response: "I have completed **Phase 2, Milestone 1: Backend Foundation**.\n\n---\n\n### File Explanations (Beginner-Friendly Guide)\n\n1. **`backend/package.json`**:\n   - Defines our backend project metadata, scripts (`npm start` and `npm run dev`), and required dependencies (`express`, `mongoose`, `dotenv`, `cors`, `cookie-parser`, `bcryptjs`, `jsonwebtoken`).\n2. **`backend/.env.example`**:\n   - A template for environment variables (`PORT`, `MONGO_URI`, `JWT_SECRET`). This ensures we never hardcode secrets in source code.\n3. **`backend/src/config/db.js`**:\n   - Uses **Mongoose** to connect our Node.js server to our MongoDB database cluster using the `MONGO_URI` connection string.\n4. **`backend/src/middleware/errorHandler.js`**:\n   - A centralized Express middleware that catches any errors occurring in our application and returns a clean, secure JSON error response.\n5. **`backend/src/server.js`**:\n   - The main entry point. It creates our Express app, applies security and parsing middleware (`cors`, `express.json`, `cookie-parser`), connects to MongoDB, provides the health-check endpoint (`GET /api/health`), attaches the error handler, and starts listening on port 5000.\n\n---\n\n### Exact Terminal Commands to Run\n\nTo test Milestone 1, open your terminal and execute the following commands inside the `backend` directory:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Navigate to the backend directory\ncd backend\n\n# 2. Install dependencies\nnpm install\n\n# 3. Create your local .env file from the template\ncp .env.example .env\n\n# 4. Start the backend server in development mode\nnpm run dev\n```\n\n---\n\n### How to Test the Health-Check Endpoint\n\nOnce the server is running, open your browser or Postman and test:\n```text\nhttp://localhost:5000/api/health\n```\n**Expected Response:**\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"UP\",\n  \"message\": \"VELoop Rewards Backend API is running successfully\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T...\"\n}\n```\n\nPlease review and test Milestone 1, and reply with your approval to proceed to **Milestone 2: Database Models & Authentication APIs**."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
