  planner_response {
    response: "I have successfully completed **Milestone 2: Database Models & Authentication APIs**.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of What Was Built\n\n1. **Mongoose Database Models (`backend/src/models/`)**:\n   - Created all required schemas: `User`, `Wallet`, `WalletTransaction`, `LevelConfig`, `Achievement`, `UserAchievement`, `Referral`, `Withdrawal`, `ActivityLog`, `AdminUser`, and `AdminAuditLog`.\n2. **Authentication Middleware (`backend/src/middleware/auth.js`)**:\n   - Implemented secure JWT verification for users and administrators (`verifyUserToken` and `verifyAdminToken`).\n3. **Authentication Controller & Routes (`backend/src/controllers/authController.js`, `backend/src/routes/authRoutes.js`)**:\n   - `POST /api/auth/register`: Hashes passwords with `bcryptjs`, creates user records, initializes wallets, and returns JWT tokens.\n   - `POST /api/auth/login`: Validates credentials and issues user session tokens.\n   - `GET /api/auth/me`: Returns current authenticated user profile.\n   - `POST /api/auth/admin/login`: Secure admin login with audit logging.\n4. **Database Seeder (`backend/src/seed.js`)**:\n   - Safely seeds initial admin credentials and default levels/achievements from environment variables without hardcoding secrets.\n\n---\n\n### Testing Instructions for Milestone 2\n\n1. Start your backend server:\n   ```bash\n   PORT=5000 node --import tsx/esm backend/src/server.js\n   ```\n2. Test user registration via `curl`:\n   ```bash\n   curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/register \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d \'{\"username\": \"Alex Vance\", \"email\": \"alex@veloop.io\", \"password\": \"password123\"}\'\n   ```\n3. Test user login:\n   ```bash\n   curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d \'{\"email\": \"alex@veloop.io\", \"password\": \"password123\"}\'\n   ```\n\nPlease review and test Milestone 2, and reply with your approval to proceed to **Milestone 3: Profile & Admin Management APIs**."
    modified_response: "I have successfully completed **Milestone 2: Database Models & Authentication APIs**.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of What Was Built\n\n1. **Mongoose Database Models (`backend/src/models/`)**:\n   - Created all required schemas: `User`, `Wallet`, `WalletTransaction`, `LevelConfig`, `Achievement`, `UserAchievement`, `Referral`, `Withdrawal`, `ActivityLog`, `AdminUser`, and `AdminAuditLog`.\n2. **Authentication Middleware (`backend/src/middleware/auth.js`)**:\n   - Implemented secure JWT verification for users and administrators (`verifyUserToken` and `verifyAdminToken`).\n3. **Authentication Controller & Routes (`backend/src/controllers/authController.js`, `backend/src/routes/authRoutes.js`)**:\n   - `POST /api/auth/register`: Hashes passwords with `bcryptjs`, creates user records, initializes wallets, and returns JWT tokens.\n   - `POST /api/auth/login`: Validates credentials and issues user session tokens.\n   - `GET /api/auth/me`: Returns current authenticated user profile.\n   - `POST /api/auth/admin/login`: Secure admin login with audit logging.\n4. **Database Seeder (`backend/src/seed.js`)**:\n   - Safely seeds initial admin credentials and default levels/achievements from environment variables without hardcoding secrets.\n\n---\n\n### Testing Instructions for Milestone 2\n\n1. Start your backend server:\n   ```bash\n   PORT=5000 node --import tsx/esm backend/src/server.js\n   ```\n2. Test user registration via `curl`:\n   ```bash\n   curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/register \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d \'{\"username\": \"Alex Vance\", \"email\": \"alex@veloop.io\", \"password\": \"password123\"}\'\n   ```\n3. Test user login:\n   ```bash\n   curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d \'{\"email\": \"alex@veloop.io\", \"password\": \"password123\"}\'\n   ```\n\nPlease review and test Milestone 2, and reply with your approval to proceed to **Milestone 3: Profile & Admin Management APIs**."
