  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding a withdrawal route**\n\nI\'m currently working on adding a `POST /profile/withdraw` route to `server/routes/api.ts`. I need to ensure the fallbackStore and DB correctly handle this new route. I\'ve begun to construct the function and will soon be testing its integration.\n\n\n**Validating Withdrawal Parameters**\n\nI\'ve just added several validation checks within the new withdrawal route. The route now verifies the provided parameters, including asset type and amount, and ensures the amount is a positive number. There\'s also a crucial asset type check to prevent unauthorized withdrawals of XP. If the DB isn\'t ready, the route utilizes the fallback store and checks for sufficient balances. I\'m now testing edge cases.\n\n\n**Implementing Fallback Storage**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating the fallback store within the withdrawal route, writing new withdrawal data, transactions, and activities. I am ensuring that new withdrawal requests are pushed to the beginning of the arrays. Currently, I\'m checking to make sure everything operates as expected when the DB is unavailable. I am planning on adding a success message with the new withdrawal, after the fallback store operations.\n\n\n**Finalizing Withdrawal Process**\n\nI\'ve just added the crucial balance and funds validation checks within the withdrawal route and added associated error messages. There are checks in place to ensure a valid and positive withdrawal amount, and that sufficient balance exists. I have also added model saving for the withdrawal. Now, I have added the withdrawal record in the WalletTransactionModel, and included a description detailing the withdrawal. Finally, an ActivityLog is created for the new withdrawal request.\n\n\n"
